      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Valley of King Xorbb [zone=875]\n**Who:**\n- Thistlebrush [ _Quests, Mission, Raid_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Large Ham Chunk [item=107987]\n- Multiphasic Facet [item=108350]\n- Multiphasic Ring [item=108352]\n- Thistlebrush's Everburning Torch [item=108343]\n- Thistlebrush's Poultice [item=108347]\n- Visibility Totem [item=108349]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Brantun [npc=42414]\n- a minotaur cook [npc=42368]\n- a minotaur shelter [npc=42369]\n- a multiphasic crystal [npc=42442]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Raid Expedition: Valley of King Xorbb [quest=6112]\n- The Battle for Rivervale [quest=6109]\n- The Return of King Xorbb [quest=6110]\n- Xorbb #1: The Halfling Trail [quest=6106]\n- Xorbb #3: Escape From the Prison of Xorbb [quest=6108]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 06:14:16 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the second in a series of three. It is a solo task that begins with Thistlebrush ( map) in the Valley of King Xorbb at location -1385, -970, 107 (a little ways north of the zone-in)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed The Halfling Trail [quest=6106]\nYou say, 'Hail, Thistlebrush'\nThistlebrush says 'Your efforts have helped us much, especially Brantun and Barleyburr when [they] were lost in the valley. Thank you!'\nThistlebrush holds out his hand toward you, and flames leap to life, dancing about on his palm. 'Brantun and Barleyburr yet live! Our hope is not lost, thanks to you!' With his other hand, Thistlebrush holds the haft of a torch and dips it into the living fire. 'But as you know, they have not escaped [danger].'\nYou say, 'What danger?'\nThistlebrush says 'Whilst goblins crowd the halls of underearth, Brantun and Barleyburr cannot emerge from hiding and descend to the seat of Xorbb. Besides, with Brantun's leg broken and Barleyburr's constant hunger gnawing at his mind, the two would not make it far. We must aid them with food and healing, but first we must create a [distraction].' Thistlebrush proffers to you the lit torch.'\nYou say, 'A distraction?'\nThistlebrush says 'We will spread pandemonium among the minotaur camps and lure the goblins to the surface to aid their fellow minions. Once the mayhem evacuates the caverns, you can deliver aid to Brantun and Barleyburr, and they can continue their journey. You will take up this torch, [right]?'\nYou say, 'Right!'\nThistlebrush hands you the torch, and his eyes gleam in its light. 'Burn the tents of the minotaurs. They will bellow with rage, and the goblins will answer their call.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'We Have to Go Deeper'.\n_You receive \"Thistlebrush's Everburning Torch\"._\nBrantun and Barleyburr have escaped the goblin cook's mallet, but now they are hiding within the goblin halls, injured and waiting for a chance to resume their quest. Thistlebrush wants you to create a distraction that will lure some of the goblins out of their halls. Then you can deliver aid to Brantun and Barleyburr.\nBy destroying minotaur tents along the western river, we can put Xorbb's forces in disarray. Goblins will come to the surface to aid the minotaurs in salvaging their encampments. Use the torch Thistlebrush gave you to light the tents on fire.\n\n---\n\nDestroy 7 of the minotaur shelters to create a diversion 0/7 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nThroughout the valley are several minotaur shelters [npc=42369] scattered about (in the various mino camps around the zone). Use the torch on these tents. When you do so, some waterbrigade goblins spawn and try to heal the tents. These goblins don't have many hitpoints and don't hit too hard for their level (max ~6,500), but they can sometimes appear in large numbers.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Thistlebrush 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tell Thistlebrush Xorbb's forces are in disarray and that you lured out the goblins.\nYou say, 'Hail, Thistlebrush'\nThistlebrush says 'The valley teems with goblins and minotaurs, as though you stamped upon an anthill. The goblin nest has emptied, and will remain so while the detritus of your handiwork has been cleared. Now is the time to deliver aid to Brantun and Barleyburr.' Thistlebrush removes a pouch from his pocket. 'This poultice will soothe Brantun's leg and give him the strength to walk, though it cannot fully restore his mobility. It is the best I can do from afar.' Thistlebrush rubs his chin for a moment. 'Barleyburr needs ham. He thrives upon it. I fear without sufficient ham supply, the plan will be ruined, for Barleyburr will be too weak to bolster Brantun's spirit, let alone his own. Having none of the meat myself, you must steal it from the minotaurs' spits. Once you have some, deliver the ham and poultice to Brantun and Barleyburr.'\nYou receive Thistlebrush's Poultice [item=108347].\n\n---\n\nKill a minotaur cook that is watching over his ham 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nSteal some ham off of a minotaur spit 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n_Task Window Says:_ Thistlebrush has given you a poultice to deliver to Brantun, but Barleyburr still needs ham to keep his strength. You will need to kill a minotaur cook and steal a piece of ham that is roasting on his spit.\nKnown spawn points for minotaur cooks [npc=42368] ( map):\n\\\\* -675, 635, -73 (south-central part of the zone; east of the north end of the large lake/waterfall)\n\\\\* 690, 195, -45 (north-central part of the zone; southeast from the architect camp - across the river)\n\\\\* 700, 730, -60 (northwestern part of the zone; southwest from the architect camp - same side of river)\n\\\\* 1025, -705, 136 (northeast from the north exit out of the crater area)\nMinotaur cooks hit for an average of 14k; AE rampage (about full damage); have a fair amount of hitpoints; and cast \"Meat Cleaver\" on random targets:\nMeat Cleaver: Single Target, Magic (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 60000\nThe spits are right next to the minotaur cooks. Click one to receive a Large Ham Chunk [item=107987].\nYou cut a piece of ham from the spit.\n\n---\n\nTell Brantun that you have created a diversion and brought supplies 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nBrantun [npc=42414] (and Barleyburr -- map) are in the underground system at around /waypoint -811,+903,-372.18 in the narrow hallway that's just west of the bar / kitchen area. He's on Find (Ctrl+F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Brantun'\nBrantun lurches at you, sword drawn, aiming steel at your throat. Barleyburr grabs Brantun's sleeve and barely restrains him from spilling your blood. Brantun speaks slowly but keeps his sword pointed at you. 'You are no goblin, but can I trust you? Many like you would think no more of killing a halfling than killing a goat. Although, you say Thistlebrush sent you?' Brantun lowers his sword but keeps his hand clenched around the hilt and his eyes narrowed. 'Then prove to us your words.'\nGive the large chunk of ham to Barleyburr 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nBarleyburr grabs the ham from your hands. His eyes widen, and a smile breaks across his face before he brings the ham to his lips and kisses it. 'The minute I saw you, I knew you were an upstanding \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, who definitely values the finer things in life! Brantun, how could you be so suspicious of \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_? Anyone who bears the gift of ham is a wonderful friend to have!' Barleyburr claps you on the shoulder. 'When this whole Xorbb business is done, all of us will sit down and share some cured ham, pints of ale, and excellent company!'\nGive Brantun the poultice for his leg 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nBrantun rolls up his pant leg and applies the poultice over the ridge of tibia poking through the skin. He stifles a cry as his skin glows and the wound begins to close. After a moment's rest, he rises and begins to walk about, limping, although more mobile than he had been. Out of breath, he addresses you. 'You spoke truthfully, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, but a slab of ham and a mended leg will not guarantee our success. Even with your diversion, I doubt we can penetrate Xorbb's heart while the eyes gaze upon us.'\nAsk Brantun what he needs to continue the quest 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nYou say, 'Hail, Brantun'\nBrantun says 'While we hid, we listened. The goblins in their tavern spoke of the eyes that watch over Xorbb's domain. They are his lieutenants and generals, his tacticians and seers. They see what you and I cannot. They penetrate even the most ancient incantations of invisibility. We will never avoid their gaze -- unless what the goblins say is true. Within the mines of crystals, which sprouted from veins touched by the heart of fear, living shards wander tunnels like ghosts, invisible even to the eyes that patrol the mines. The miners told tales of these wraithlike crystals flickering into existence before vanishing once more, and many miners are afraid to work alone. If we could manage to obtain pieces of these crystals, Thistlebrush might be able to extract their power and give to us a means to avoid the eyes.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Thistlebrush 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tell Thistlebrush that Brantun and Barleyburr cannot make it past the eyes of Xorbb unseen. Brantun overheard goblins saying that pieces of living crystal shards in the crystal mines can blind in and out of existence. Thistlebrush might know how to harness this power.\nYou say, 'Hail, Thistlebrush'\nThistlebrush looks into the distance. His eyes appear glassy, and he slowly nods while he speaks. 'What Brantun describes must be powerful magic, elemental in its form. The heart of fear must have spread roots throughout this valley, and even the rocks and soil bear its seed. I know a spell -- I do not know its origin, so ancient is it -- that might reveal to you that which cannot be seen.' Thistlebrush holds out his hand. A cloud as black as midnight begins to swirl around Thistlebrush's palm, and a small idol takes shape in his hand. 'Place this upon the ground, and the hidden becomes visible. Go now to the crystal mines. Brantun and Barleyburr depend upon what you discover!\"\nYou receive a Visibility Totem [item=108349].\n\n---\n\nLoot 4 Multiphasic Facets from multiphasic crystals 0/4 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n_Task Window Says:_ Thistlebrush has given you a totem of ancient magic that might reveal the unseen creatures of crystal. In the crystal mines to the west, drop a totem, reveal the hidden beings, and try to take pieces of crystal from their bodies after you kill them.\nGo to the mining/crystal area of the underground system (these are the caves in the northernmost part of your map). Right-clicking the Visibility Totem spawns an aura in place. Mobs called a multiphasic crystal [npc=42442] wander the entirety of the crystal mines, but they are only visible and attackable if they are in one of these auras. In order to kill one, it has to be kept inside the aura until its death.\nOnce a totem is dropped on the ground, it generates an aura with a fair range. If you have multiple group members on this step, you can set it up so that you have a large range. Keep an eye out for \"a multiphasic crystal\" (hyrda model) to appear. These roam through the tunnels.\na multiphasic crystal\" is not KOS and not social with anything else (including each other).\nThey don't hit hard (a max ~7,000); flurry; are belly casters (stand on them to land spells); and have a series of emotes that lead up to an AE (they keep cycling through them until dead):\na multiphasic crystal's first head begins to glow.\na multiphasic crystal's second head begins to glow.\na multiphasic crystal's third head begins to glow.\na multiphasic crystal's heads discharge their energy. _(\"Triphobic Discharge\" is cast)_\na multiphasic crystal's heads are drained of power.\nTriphobic Discharge: PB AE 55', Prismatic (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 70000\n2: 20% Chance to trigger: Triphobia\nTriphobia\" is a 60-second fear.\nThey drop 1-3 crystals per kill.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Thistlebrush 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nYou say, 'Hail, Thistlebrush'\nThistlebrush's face darkens, as though a cloud were passing overhead. 'These crystals do not belong to this world.' He covers them inside his hands, and a black glow emanates from the cracks between his fingers. Revealing his palms, he displays to you two rings forged of the crystal. Darkness seems to hang about Thistlebrush's head, and he speaks slowly. 'With these rings, Brantun and Barleyburr will walk in the realm of the crystal. The eyes will not see them. But I cannot say who or what else might be watching when the rings encompass their fingers. Go now. Regardless the cost, we must see this matter to the end.'\nYou receive 2x Multiphasic Ring [item=108352].\n\n---\n\nGive a Multiphasic Ring to Brantun 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nGive a Multiphasic Ring to Barleyburr 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n_Task Window Says:_ Using some strange power, Thistlebrush has fused the crystals into rings. Wearers of the rings will possess the power of invisibility. Now Brantun and Barleyburr will be able to avoid the eyes of Xorbb.\nBarleyburr shudders as you hand him the ring. 'Must we wear such a thing, Brantun? It is heavy, unnatural...' Barleyburr places the ring in his pack, and weight seems to lift from him. 'We best get to moving now. The sooner we finish our journey, the sooner we enjoy that feast, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!'\nBrantun says 'So the shards exist...I did not know Thistlebrush's abilities were so advanced as to harness a power such as this.' Brantun holds the ring in his hand, and his visage grows darker, even under torchlight. 'It is heavier than it looks.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Brantun 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\nYou say, 'Hail, Brantun'\nBrantun says 'Thank you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Await our message. When we near the heart of Xorbb's power, we will call for Thistlebrush to execute his final stratagem. The next time we meet, I pray it is above ground!'\nYou have succeeded in bringing aid to Brantun and Barleyburr. With the tunnels evacuated of many goblins, and with the rings you have given Brantun and Barleyburr, they can now make their way toward Xorbb's seat of power. Stay in contact with Thistlebrush to know when Brantun and Barleyburr send their final message.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (3 AAs + 2-3% in Level 98)",
    },
