      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Valley of King Xorbb [zone=875]\n**Who:**\n- a dying scout [npc=41359]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Box of Captured Lightning [item=109028]\n- Empty Lightning Box [item=109000]\n- Hollowflesh Golem [item=109035]\n- Minotaur Head [item=108344]\n- Minotaur Limb [item=108377]\n- Minotaur Torso [item=108670]\n- Runed Coffin [item=109034]\n- Wiry Pondweed [item=108869]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dabbin Sneakfoot [npc=42415]\n- Grolak the Ancient [npc=42418]\n- a cloudburst cyclone [npc=42327]\n- a cloudburst whirlwind [npc=42328]\n- a halfling prisoner [npc=42361]\n- a shamanic minotaur [npc=42151]\n- a warrior minotaur [npc=42398]\n- a watchman minotaur [npc=42399]\n- an overseer minotaur [npc=42412]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 10:11:02 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with \"a dying scout\" ( map) in the Valley of King Xorbb. She is located in the underground system at -1210, 415, -402. She's found in the main passageway (with the river flowing through the center) just southwest of the prison (which is the large circular room in the under ground system's southeastern area)._\nYou say, 'Hail, a dying scout'\na dying scout says 'Who...? No. I must be hallucinating. I'm just... Seeing things. Why would a \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ be here? You can't be [real]. \\*sigh\\*'\nYou say, 'Of course I'm real'\na dying scout says 'Then maybe... I'm being given a second chance?... I was supposed to scout out the pit and learn what I could... but I've failed... This mission has cost me my life... But if I don't finish, it will cost more lives... Please! Will you [carry out] this mission in my place?'\nYou say, 'I'll carry out the mission!'\na dying scout says 'Thank you!... please, find out what's going on in the pit and report it to Dabbin, near the tunnel to the Gorge... and ask him... to look after my little 'lings, and tell them I love them...'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Plans Gone Awry'.\nBefore dying, a Halfling scout asked you to carry out her final mission. Find out what's going on inside the pit, and report to Dabbin Sneakfoot, who waits near the tunnel to the gorge.\n\n---\n\n03. Try talking to one of the imprisoned Halflings 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Speak to one of the \"a halfling prisoner\" ( map) mobs in any of the cells that surround the large circular room east of the dying scout's location._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a halfling prisoner'\n\n\n\n\na halfling prisoner says 'How did you get in here? Have you come to [free] us?!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'I can't free you...'\n\n\n\n\na halfling prisoner says 'What? Oh... I see. I'm sorry to hear that. \\*sigh\\* Well, if it's information you need, at least, I think I can help. But in exchange, please tell Dabbin about our plight. [Agreed]?'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Agreed!'\n\n\n\n\na halfling prisoner says 'Alright, it's a deal; we'll hold strong until help comes and help you all we can in the meantime. Now, the best person to give you information would be one of the Goblins which run this place - although I doubt if any of them would willingly comply with such a request - but, I've got an [idea] how we can get around that.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'What idea?'\n\n\n\n\na halfling prisoner says 'There's a Goblin, by the name of Grolak, who's nearly blind with old age. I've seen him mistake both Halflings and the undead monstrosities here for fellow Goblins! If you approach him pretending to be a Goblin, he may just fall for it.'\n\n04. Speak with Grolak the Ancient 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Grolak the Ancient ( map) is found in one of the southeast prison cells (-1125, 75, -430)._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Grolak the Ancient'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says 'Eh? What? Were you raised by werewolves or something?! Don't you know it's rude to address your elders in that hideous, \"Common\" tongue?! You kids today! I suppose next you'll all be skipping around dressed like Halflings! \\*sigh\\* Oh well. I suppose it's not all your fault; I'll yell at your parents later. Now - I take it you're my new apprentice, [yes]?'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Yes, of course'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says 'Right then. Now, we'll need [lightning], some [minotaur parts], and something to bind the parts together. Hmm... [pondweed] should do! Naturally, as my apprentice, it's up to you to collect these - hah! I hope you're up to it.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Lightning?'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says 'I don't hold with these modern, lightning-free reanimation spells kids use nowadays. In MY day, we used to wait WEEKS for a good thunderstorm - and we were GRATEFUL when one arrived! \\*sigh\\* But we're short on thunderstorms here, so we'll have to make do with what we can steal from the dervishes in the valley. You can use this box to store the lightning from cloudburst whirlwinds or cyclones.'\n\n\n\n\n_You receive \"Empty Lightning Box\"._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Minotaur parts?'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says 'Oh, just about anything will work. Preferably a few heads, though. Tough as rocks those things are - which is about how clever the beasts are, anyway. You'll find most of the lazy things in the valley above, grazing and fertilizing the fields. Just be sure to leave no witnesses! If they notice some of their herd is missing, we'll blame it on the Halflings.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Pondweed?'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says 'There's a lake near the waterfall in the valley. Just try not to drown yourself while gathering those plants,' he sniggers maliciously, 'After all, it'd be a waste of perfectly good weeds.'\n\n\n\n\n_This opens up the next five steps._\n\n05. Use your Empty Lightning Box to steal lightning from a cloudburst dervish 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Right-click the box on \"a cloudburst whirlwind\" or \"a cloudburst cyclone\" (these spawn in the forest area east of the zone-in)._\n\n06. Loot 3 Minotaur Head 0/3 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n07. Loot 1 Minotaur Torso 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n08. Loot 3 Minotaur Limb 0/3 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n09. Gather 3 Wiry Pondweeds from the lake in the valley 0/3 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Wiry Pondweed is a ground spawn in the lake in the southeastern part of the zone (and at the bottom of the waterfall). There are many ground spawns._\n\n10. Report to Grolak the Ancient 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n11. Follow Grolak's instructions to assemble your golem 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Combine 3x minotaur head, 1x minotaur torso, 3x minotaur limb, and 3x pondweed inside the Runed Coffin._\n\n12. Deliver 1 Hollowflesh Golem to Grolak the Ancient 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient gives a few experimental tugs on the golem's limbs, 'Hmm... you're quite a natural! Most beginners try to bind the entire body the same way, and wind up with loosely joined limbs which fall off, or joints bound too tightly to move. There's good strength and flexibility in this one, though, so let's go to the [next step].'\n\n13. Listen to Grolak's instructions 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\nYou say, 'What next step?'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says, in Goblin, 'I've set it up now, so pay close attention: I'm going to reanimate the golem and I'll need you to unleash that lightning on it at the right moment. Unfortunately, however, I'll be busy casting my spell, and won't be able to talk. You'll need to watch carefully for my signal, so let me know when you're [ready].'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Ready!'\n\n14. On Grolakâ€™s signal use the Box of Captured Lightning on the golem 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_When Grolak emotes..._\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient glances in your direction, and nods his head violently: now!\n\n\n\n\n_...click the Charged Box of Lightning._\n\n15. Speak to Grolak 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Grolak the Ancient'\n\n\n\n\nGrolak the Ancient says, in Goblin, 'Hmm, not bad. Although you took forever with that lightning!' He glares accusingly at you, 'I'm sure you'll do better next time, won't you? Good. Now run along. I need to rest these old bones of mine, before I end up like our new friend here!'\n\n16. Report to Dabbin 0/1 (Valley of King Xorbb)\n\n\n\n_Dabbin Sneakfoot ( map) is found just west of the zone-in._\n\n\n---\n\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (3 AAs)",
